author He Fangyu <fangyu.he@samsung.com> 1788834097 +0800
committer He Fangyu <fangyu.he@samsung.com> 1788834097 +0800

    libcxx: match timed-wait aliases to the target intmax_t ABI
    
    The chrono ratio parameters use intmax_t. Its Itanium name encodes long
    on the supported LP64 target but long long on armv7l. The original alias
    spelling exported the LP64 name on ARM as well, so normal timed-wait
    callers failed to link despite a successful shared-library build.
    
    Select the spelling from the target long width and assert the exact
    intmax_t type at compile time. Keep both version contracts, native-handle
    access and all waiting algorithms unchanged. This is a follow-up fix;
    the previously published implementation commits are not rewritten.
    
    Validation: compare both aliases against each architecture's actual
    single-version baseline export, and rebuild both complete runtimes.
    The original ARM link failure and the independent undefined-symbol
    comparison are retained with the two-architecture validation evidence.
    Evidence: https://github.com/lhmax2010/libc-_replacement/tree/codex/runtime-validation/docs/progress/IMPL_0908/W3
    
    中文说明：ARM 的 ratio 非类型参数使用 long long，符号编码为 x；原先
    复用 x86_64 的 l 编码导致定时等待调用方无法链接。按目标类型选择并做
    静态断言，不改版本契约、等待算法或既有提交；失败原文与逐架构旧库对照保留。
